{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 2840 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "f029f064d2ac381c840e66c8f2248914098b9ee69aa9ced91288fdabd6574b37" :edb/db-before-t 2839 :edb/db-after-t 2840 :edb/tx-data [[13194139536152 50 #inst "2026-10-09T17:14:01.239Z" 13194139536152 true] [17592186129214 1020 #edb/ref 17592186386273 13194139536152 true] [17592186129214 1020 #edb/ref 17592186386280 13194139536152 true] [17592186129215 1020 #edb/ref 17592186386259 13194139536152 true] [17592186129215 1020 #edb/ref 17592186386266 13194139536152 true] [17592186129215 1020 #edb/ref 17592186386287 13194139536152 true] [17592186386259 1017 #edb/ref 17592186386260 13194139536152 true] [17592186386259 1089 "q-162236" 13194139536152 true] [17592186386259 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139536152 true] [17592186386259 1100 "Evaluate\n${\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{x}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{xy}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{4})\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.$\n\n*Hint: First change the order of integration to $\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.$*" 13194139536152 true] [17592186386259 1113 #uuid "9383b3a9-2a6a-5e82-a4da-b4d00cab688d" 13194139536152 true] [17592186386259 1145 "We wish to find the limits of integration such that our integral can be expressed as \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}{\\int }_{{v}_{1}(y)}^{{v}_{2}(y)}{\\int }_{{u}_{1}(x,y)}^{{u}_{2}(x,y)}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{4})\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.\n$$\n\nFrom the repeated integral, we see that the domain of integration $R$ can be written as a type I region as follows:\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,x\\le y\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le z\\le xy}\n$$\n\nSince all repeated integrals first integrate with respect to $z,$ the $z$-limits remain the same as before:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}{\\int }_{{v}_{1}(y)}^{{v}_{2}(y)}{\\int }_{0}^{xy}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{4})\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we consider the projection $D$ of $R$ onto the $xy$-plane shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081417/assets/6b3720af66e81aef6792d4b2a34b2bdf2b93bd59ed6e28e4b38a1e06964bb2cc.png)\n\nThe region $D$ is type I region in the $xy$-plane:\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,x\\le y\\le 1}.\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration from $\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x$ to $\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y,$ we write $D$ as a type II region.\n\nNotice that the left boundary of the region $D$ is\n\n$$\nx=0\n$$\n\nand the right boundary of the region, written in the form $x=x(y),$ is\n\n$$\ny=x\\,⟹\\,x=y.\n$$\n\nThen, the type II representation of the region is\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,0\\le x\\le y},\n$$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081417/assets/9dc99cc0df9f089b9f62402c3c5ea9c4408be077debbf6dfadeb884ee4d8b2d0.png)\n\nTherefore, by swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{x}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{xy}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{4})\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{y}{\\int }_{0}^{xy}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{4})\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{y}[{\\int }_{0}^{xy}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{4})\\,\\text{d}z]\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{y}2\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{4})[z]_{0}^{xy}\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{y}2xy\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{4})\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}y\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{4})[{\\int }_{0}^{y}2x\\,\\text{d}x]\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}y\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{4})[{x}^{2}]_{0}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{y}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡({y}^{4})\\,\\text{d}y \\\\  & ={[-\\frac{1}{4}\\operatorname{cos}⁡({y}^{4})]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{1}{4}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1)-1) \\\\  & =\\frac{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1)}{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536152 true] [17592186386260 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386261 13194139536152 true] [17592186386260 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386262 13194139536152 true] [17592186386260 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386263 13194139536152 true] [17592186386260 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386264 13194139536152 true] [17592186386260 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386265 13194139536152 true] [17592186386260 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536152 true] [17592186386260 1041 "selection" 13194139536152 true] [17592186386260 1104 #edb/ref 17592186386262 13194139536152 true] [17592186386260 1110 #uuid "04f0cf81-6deb-5a07-b103-b225b644ed8e" 13194139536152 true] [17592186386261 1034 "\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2)}{4}" 13194139536152 true] [17592186386261 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536152 true] [17592186386261 1111 #uuid "126ee6ef-6165-57b6-97c8-664b9874c753" 13194139536152 true] [17592186386262 1034 "\\frac{1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1)}{4}" 13194139536152 true] [17592186386262 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536152 true] [17592186386262 1111 #uuid "5c0041a7-89cc-5de9-a27d-d628360922b1" 13194139536152 true] [17592186386263 1034 "\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1)}{2}" 13194139536152 true] [17592186386263 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536152 true] [17592186386263 1111 #uuid "756884bf-a7d3-53d9-8b5e-67ac64c13127" 13194139536152 true] [17592186386264 1034 "2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(1)-1" 13194139536152 true] [17592186386264 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536152 true] [17592186386264 1111 #uuid "d601aed8-7270-5e56-814b-f8674a8dc5b2" 13194139536152 true] [17592186386265 1034 "1-\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2)" 13194139536152 true] [17592186386265 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536152 true] [17592186386265 1111 #uuid "04998379-a1f1-504a-9863-3cab2b7a3d10" 13194139536152 true] [17592186386266 1017 #edb/ref 17592186386267 13194139536152 true] [17592186386266 1089 "q-162250" 13194139536152 true] [17592186386266 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139536152 true] [17592186386266 1100 "Evaluate\n${\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡y}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{{e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}}\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y.$\n\n*Hint: First change the order of integration to $\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.$*" 13194139536152 true] [17592186386266 1113 #uuid "3f89ba26-5dec-5dd6-9021-9b421647a5f6" 13194139536152 true] [17592186386266 1145 "We wish to find the limits of integration such that our integral can be expressed as \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}{\\int }_{{v}_{1}(x)}^{{v}_{2}(x)}{\\int }_{{u}_{1}(x,y)}^{{u}_{2}(x,y)}\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nFrom the repeated integral, we see that the domain of integration $R$ can be written as a type I region as follows:\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,\\,\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡y\\le x\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2},\\,\\,0\\le z\\le {e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}}\n$$\n\nSince all repeated integrals first integrate with respect to $z,$ the $z$-limits remain the same as before:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}{\\int }_{{v}_{1}(x)}^{{v}_{2}(x)}{\\int }_{0}^{{e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}}\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we consider the projection $D$ of $R$ onto the $xy$-plane shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081417/assets/38eb7316b1ee5c947eee37a9cc10530ff08f793b7564cf0d88c6ce24e1239f9d.png)\n\nThe region $D$ is type II region in the $xy$-plane:\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le y\\le 1,\\,\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡y\\le x\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2}}.\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration from $\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y$ to $\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x,$ we write $D$ as a type I region.\n\nNotice that the top boundary of the region, written in the form $y=y(x),$ is\n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡y\\,⟹\\,y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\n$$\n\nand the bottom boundary of the region $D$ is\n\n$$\ny=0.\n$$\n\nThen, the type I representation of the region is\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le \\frac{\\pi }{2},\\,0\\le y\\le \\operatorname{sin}⁡x},\n$$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081417/assets/241abff7fae5d6ba3301d605ff4c4e62ff61e423515c7bc3a54b17b9aec525aa.png)\n\nTherefore, by swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡y}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{{e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}}\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}y & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{\\int }_{0}^{{e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}}\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}[{\\int }_{0}^{{e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}}\\text{d}z]\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}[z]_{0}^{{e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}[{\\int }_{0}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\text{d}y]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}[y]_{0}^{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}{e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}\\operatorname{sin}⁡x\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =[-{e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}]_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =-({e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi /2}-{e}^{\\operatorname{cos}⁡0}) \\\\  & =-(1-e) \\\\  & =e-1.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536152 true] [17592186386267 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386268 13194139536152 true] [17592186386267 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386269 13194139536152 true] [17592186386267 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386270 13194139536152 true] [17592186386267 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386271 13194139536152 true] [17592186386267 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386272 13194139536152 true] [17592186386267 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536152 true] [17592186386267 1041 "selection" 13194139536152 true] [17592186386267 1104 #edb/ref 17592186386268 13194139536152 true] [17592186386267 1110 #uuid "6be2c5db-bc7b-5e26-9d57-b6b887c43d78" 13194139536152 true] [17592186386268 1034 "e-1" 13194139536152 true] [17592186386268 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536152 true] [17592186386268 1111 #uuid "2a359fd9-52a3-59a1-a43b-54f2913795e7" 13194139536152 true] [17592186386269 1034 "{e}^{\\pi /2}" 13194139536152 true] [17592186386269 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536152 true] [17592186386269 1111 #uuid "71e427b7-ce60-5c33-80b8-33eb896da100" 13194139536152 true] [17592186386270 1034 "{e}^{\\pi }+2" 13194139536152 true] [17592186386270 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536152 true] [17592186386270 1111 #uuid "dd71d117-be4d-5736-980a-8d5eeaedea69" 13194139536152 true] [17592186386271 1034 "4" 13194139536152 true] [17592186386271 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536152 true] [17592186386271 1111 #uuid "b0a2e4c5-6464-5bc3-9cba-4413e7f21c84" 13194139536152 true] [17592186386272 1034 "2e+1" 13194139536152 true] [17592186386272 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536152 true] [17592186386272 1111 #uuid "8fbebbe5-164c-5507-9979-faef0f7d3ad3" 13194139536152 true] [17592186386273 1017 #edb/ref 17592186386274 13194139536152 true] [17592186386273 1089 "q-162322" 13194139536152 true] [17592186386273 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139536152 true] [17592186386273 1100 "By changing the order of integration, find the missing limits in the following repeated integral.\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{z}}^{{e}^{z}}{\\int }_{{z}^{2}-1}^{x+z}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{p}{\\int }_{{z}^{2}-1}^{x+z}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{q}{\\int }_{r}^{1}{\\int }_{{z}^{2}-1}^{x+z}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x\n$$" 13194139536152 true] [17592186386273 1113 #uuid "9a894708-53b5-506d-832d-c14b94f740a4" 13194139536152 true] [17592186386273 1145 "We wish to find the limits of integration such that our integral can be expressed as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}{\\int }_{{v}_{1}(x)}^{{v}_{2}(x)}{\\int }_{{u}_{1}(x,z)}^{{u}_{2}(x,z)}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{c}^{d}{\\int }_{{v}_{3}(x)}^{{v}_{4}(x)}{\\int }_{{u}_{3}(x,z)}^{{u}_{4}(x,z)}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nFrom the repeated integral, we see that the domain of integration $R$ can be written as a type III region as follows:\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le z\\le 1,\\,\\,\\sqrt{z}\\le x\\le {e}^{z},\\,\\,{z}^{2}-1\\le y\\le x+z}\n$$\n\nSince all repeated integrals first integrate with respect to $y,$ the $y$-limits remain the same as before:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{\\sqrt{z}}^{{e}^{z}}{\\int }_{{z}^{2}-1}^{x+z}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z={\\int }_{a}^{b}{\\int }_{{v}_{1}(x)}^{{v}_{2}(x)}{\\int }_{{z}^{2}-1}^{x+z}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{c}^{d}{\\int }_{{v}_{3}(x)}^{{v}_{4}(x)}{\\int }_{{z}^{2}-1}^{x+z}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we consider the projection $D$ of $R$ onto the $xz$-plane shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081417/assets/41b06d98498273a03b9df8eeaa60f4e74cb00168e8dd0b3b395c5b0a23518e57.png)\n\nThe region $D$ is a type II region in the $xz$-plane:\n\n$$\nD={(x,z)\\,:\\,0\\le z\\le 1,\\,\\sqrt{z}\\le x\\le {e}^{z}}.\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration from $\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z$ to $\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x,$ we split $D$ into two type I regions.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081417/assets/07a37b90df8b37d07c40af03ecba8e665797cfff368758db7ae17e45f11683cf.png)\n\nNotice that the bottom and top boundaries of the left region, written in the form $z=z(x),$ are\n\n$\\,$ $z=0\\,$ and $\\,z={x}^{2}.$\n\nAlso, the bottom and top boundaries of the right region, written in the form $z=z(x),$ are\n\n$\\,$ $z=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\,$ and $\\,z=1.$\n\nSo, we can write $D$ as a union of\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}={(x,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le z\\le {x}^{2}}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n{D}_{2}={(x,z)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le e,\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\le z\\le 1}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, by swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{{x}^{2}}{\\int }_{{z}^{2}-1}^{x+z}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{1}^{e}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}^{1}{\\int }_{{z}^{2}-1}^{x+z}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536152 true] [17592186386274 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386275 13194139536152 true] [17592186386274 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386276 13194139536152 true] [17592186386274 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386277 13194139536152 true] [17592186386274 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386278 13194139536152 true] [17592186386274 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386279 13194139536152 true] [17592186386274 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536152 true] [17592186386274 1041 "selection" 13194139536152 true] [17592186386274 1104 #edb/ref 17592186386278 13194139536152 true] [17592186386274 1110 #uuid "6ee971d1-e5fa-579d-859c-0e1f92aa1289" 13194139536152 true] [17592186386275 1034 "p={x}^{2},\\,\\,\\,q=2,\\,\\,\\,r=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x" 13194139536152 true] [17592186386275 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536152 true] [17592186386275 1111 #uuid "108be47a-4b65-5e38-9757-e88fedddeff6" 13194139536152 true] [17592186386276 1034 "p=\\sqrt{x},\\,\\,\\,q=e,\\,\\,\\,r=x" 13194139536152 true] [17592186386276 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536152 true] [17592186386276 1111 #uuid "d2cbe476-e1f7-55af-a343-2aec7c66279f" 13194139536152 true] [17592186386277 1034 "p=2x,\\,\\,\\,q=2,\\,\\,\\,r={e}^{x}" 13194139536152 true] [17592186386277 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536152 true] [17592186386277 1111 #uuid "6c0776f3-d984-5b03-9583-5f53c92af266" 13194139536152 true] [17592186386278 1034 "p={x}^{2},\\,\\,\\,q=e,\\,\\,\\,r=\\operatorname{ln}⁡x" 13194139536152 true] [17592186386278 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536152 true] [17592186386278 1111 #uuid "1b962d52-e18a-597c-9a07-375c4fb8f919" 13194139536152 true] [17592186386279 1034 "p=2x,\\,\\,\\,q=e,\\,\\,\\,r={e}^{x}" 13194139536152 true] [17592186386279 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536152 true] [17592186386279 1111 #uuid "e4faaba5-05d2-5f8e-855c-4cdfcb933599" 13194139536152 true] [17592186386280 1017 #edb/ref 17592186386281 13194139536152 true] [17592186386280 1089 "q-162323" 13194139536152 true] [17592186386280 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139536152 true] [17592186386280 1100 "By changing the order of integration, find the missing limits in the following repeated integral.\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{(x+1)^{3}}^{2-{x}^{2}}{\\int }_{x+z}^{z+2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{0}^{p}{\\int }_{q}^{\\sqrt[3]{z}-1}{\\int }_{x+z}^{z+2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z+{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{r}^{0}{\\int }_{x+z}^{z+2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z\n$$" 13194139536152 true] [17592186386280 1113 #uuid "3c6a7892-f379-54dc-a908-63706fadb5c6" 13194139536152 true] [17592186386280 1145 "We wish to find the limits of integration such that our integral can be expressed as\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}{\\int }_{{v}_{1}(z)}^{{v}_{2}(z)}{\\int }_{{u}_{1}(x,z)}^{{u}_{2}(x,z)}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z+{\\int }_{c}^{d}{\\int }_{{v}_{3}(z)}^{{v}_{4}(z)}{\\int }_{{u}_{3}(x,z)}^{{u}_{4}(x,z)}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z.\n$$\n\nFrom the repeated integral, we see that the domain of integration $R$ can be written as a type III region as follows:\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,-1\\le x\\le 0,\\,\\,(x+1)^{3}\\le z\\le 2-{x}^{2},\\,\\,x+z\\le y\\le z+2}\n$$\n\nSince all repeated integrals first integrate with respect to $y,$ the $y$-limits remain the same as before:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{-1}^{0}{\\int }_{(x+1)^{3}}^{2-{x}^{2}}{\\int }_{x+z}^{z+2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x={\\int }_{a}^{b}{\\int }_{{v}_{1}(z)}^{{v}_{2}(z)}{\\int }_{x+z}^{z+2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z+{\\int }_{c}^{d}{\\int }_{{v}_{3}(z)}^{{v}_{4}(z)}{\\int }_{x+z}^{z+2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we consider the projection $D$ of $R$ onto the $xz$-plane shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081417/assets/5f586edef4202e3f3de09fe947c955de62efa35e421e85b3e5034efd375790a7.png)\n\nThe region $D$ is a type I region in the $xz$-plane:\n\n$$\nD={(x,y)\\,:\\,-1\\le x\\le 0,\\,(x+1)^{3}\\le z\\le 2-{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration from $\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x$ to $\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z,$ we split $D$ into two type II regions.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081417/assets/ec9845e347959ff1ac43a12d03261b1eb31172f14b56269d7bbfcb86a2a23e48.png)\n\nNotice that the bottom and top boundaries of the lower region, written in the form $x=x(z),$ are\n\n$\\,$ $x=-1\\,$ and $\\,x=\\sqrt[3]{z}-1.$\n\nAlso, the bottom and top boundaries of the upper region, written in the form $x=x(z),$ are\n\n$\\,$ $x=-\\sqrt{2-z}\\,$ and $\\,x=0.$\n\nSo, we can write $D$ as a union of\n\n$$\n{D}_{1}={(x,z)\\,:\\,0\\le z\\le 1,\\,-1\\le x\\le \\sqrt[3]{z}-1}\n$$\n\nand\n\n$$\n{D}_{2}={(x,z)\\,:\\,1\\le z\\le 2,\\,-\\sqrt{2-z}\\le x\\le 0}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, by swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-1}^{\\sqrt[3]{z}-1}{\\int }_{x+z}^{z+2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z+{\\int }_{1}^{2}{\\int }_{-\\sqrt{2-z}}^{0}{\\int }_{x+z}^{z+2}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536152 true] [17592186386281 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386282 13194139536152 true] [17592186386281 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386283 13194139536152 true] [17592186386281 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386284 13194139536152 true] [17592186386281 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386285 1319413953