0c1e-5ce3-8b80-1b84145bbf51" 13194139536152 true] [17592186386287 1145 "We wish to find the limits of integration such that our integral can be expressed as \n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}{\\int }_{{v}_{1}(x)}^{{v}_{2}(x)}{\\int }_{{u}_{1}(x,z)}^{{u}_{2}(x,z)}z{e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nFrom the repeated integral, we see that the domain of integration $R$ can be written as a type III region as follows:\n\n$$\nR={(x,y,z)\\,:\\,0\\le z\\le 1,\\,\\,z\\le x\\le 1,\\,\\,0\\le y\\le {x}^{3}}\n$$\n\nSince all repeated integrals first integrate with respect to $y,$ the $y$-limits remain the same as before:\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{a}^{b}{\\int }_{{v}_{1}(x)}^{{v}_{2}(x)}{\\int }_{0}^{{x}^{3}}z{e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, we consider the projection $D$ of $R$ onto the $xz$-plane shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081417/assets/54d8420870ea92e42811a13ed2c4563c5c9ccb674ee8c3b6a277186c0fba21da.png)\n\nThe region $D$ is type II region in the $xz$-plane:\n\n$$\nD={(x,z)\\,:\\,0\\le z\\le 1,\\,z\\le x\\le 1}.\n$$\n\nTo change the order of integration from $\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z$ to $\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x,$ we write $D$ as a type I region.\n\nNotice that the top boundary of the region $D,$ written in the form $z=z(x),$ is\n\n$$\nx=z\\,⟹\\,z=x\n$$\n\nand the bottom boundary of the region $D$ is\n\n$$\nz=0.\n$$\n\nThen, the type I representation of the region is\n\n$$\nD={(x,z)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,0\\le z\\le x},\n$$\n\nas shown in the diagram below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14081417/assets/7f19b63139a3d38c321e9938c1e8fbbf84e924df51d9b9b057d0151fc269550d.png)\n\nTherefore, by swapping the order of integration, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{z}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{{x}^{3}}z{e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}x\\,\\text{d}z & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{x}{\\int }_{0}^{{x}^{3}}z{e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{x}[z{\\int }_{0}^{{x}^{3}}{e}^{y}\\,\\text{d}y]\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{x}z[{e}^{y}]_{0}^{{x}^{3}}\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{0}^{x}z({e}^{{x}^{3}}-1)\\,\\text{d}z\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}[({e}^{{x}^{3}}-1){\\int }_{0}^{x}z\\,\\text{d}z]\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}({e}^{{x}^{3}}-1){[\\frac{1}{2}{z}^{2}]}_{0}^{x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{2}({e}^{{x}^{3}}-1)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{x}^{2}{e}^{{x}^{3}}-{x}^{2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{[\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{{x}^{3}}-\\frac{1}{3}{x}^{3}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}[e-1-1+0] \\\\  & =\\frac{e-2}{6}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139536152 true] [17592186386288 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386289 13194139536152 true] [17592186386288 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386290 13194139536152 true] [17592186386288 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386291 13194139536152 true] [17592186386288 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386292 13194139536152 true] [17592186386288 1000 #edb/ref 17592186386293 13194139536152 true] [17592186386288 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139536152 true] [17592186386288 1041 "selection" 13194139536152 true] [17592186386288 1104 #edb/ref 17592186386293 13194139536152 true] [17592186386288 1110 #uuid "c0170ff8-6b02-576b-8f7d-de381dbc8e3a" 13194139536152 true] [17592186386289 1034 "2e" 13194139536152 true] [17592186386289 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536152 true] [17592186386289 1111 #uuid "5690a51c-c8ed-5722-b7f4-04339169433a" 13194139536152 true] [17592186386290 1034 "\\frac{e}{4}" 13194139536152 true] [17592186386290 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139536152 true] [17592186386290 1111 #uuid "dadf3d2b-7ec9-560d-a4d8-80219b61e0bc" 13194139536152 true] [17592186386291 1034 "2" 13194139536152 true] [17592186386291 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 131